ginkgo
------------------------------------------
Ginkgo is a high-performance linear algebra library for manycore systems, with
a focus on sparse solution of linear systems. It is implemented using modern
C++ (you will need at least C++14 compliant compiler to build it), with GPU
kernels implemented in CUDA and HIP.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libginkgo-devel-1.11.0-1bl1
  libginkgo1.11.0-1.11.0-1bl1
  libgomp1-14.4.0-1
  libmetis0-5.2.1-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.9-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.4-1
  cygport-0.37.11-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libgflags-devel-2.2.2-1
  libgklib-devel-5.1.1-1+git8bd6bad
  libgtest-devel-1.18.0-1bl1
  libmetis-devel-5.2.1-1
  libopenmpi-devel-4.1.6-1
  libyaml-cpp-devel-0.9.0-1bl2
  ninja-1.13.2-1
  nlohmann_json-3.12.0-1bl3

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/ginkgo-project/ginkgo

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/ginkgo-project/ginkgo/archive/refs/tags/v1.11.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack ginkgo-1.11.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./ginkgo-1.11.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/ginkgo-1.11.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/ginkgo-1.11.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libginkgo1.11.0-1.11.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libginkgo-devel-1.11.0-X.tar.xz

